{"id": "sonnet__GEN__omni_1790__0", "result": "Factor 101101101101 step by step.\n\n1. Since 101 \u00d7 1001001001 = 101101101101, we have 101101101101 = 101 \u00d7 1001001001.\n2. 1001001001 = 10\u2079 + 10\u2076 + 10\u00b3 + 1 = (10\u00b3 + 1)(10\u2076 + 1) = 1001 \u00d7 1000001.\n3. 1001 = 7 \u00d7 11 \u00d7 13.\n4. 1000001 = 101 \u00d7 9901, and 9901 is a known prime.\n\nSo 101101101101 = 7 \u00d7 11 \u00d7 13 \u00d7 101\u00b2 \u00d7 9901. The largest prime factor is 9901.\n\nANSWER: 9901", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.01083, "model_used": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "secs": 10.8}